 "final_text": "**Answer: the AP subledger is the blocker, off by $2,500.**\n\nWhat I found for CESP (CES Programs LLC) February close:\n\n| Subledger | ERP open balance | Workbook balance | GL account | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| AR | $128,500 | $128,500 | 130100 | tied |\n| AP | $80,500 | $78,000 | 200100 | **in progress \u2014 not tied** |\n| Cash | \u2014 | $412,300 | 110100 | tied |\n\n- ERP AP subledger (open vendor invoices, `VendorTransactions` for CESP) sums to **$80,500** (3 open invoices: stage buildout $28,000, February freight $19,500, AV equipment rental $33,000).\n- The close reconciliation workbook (`CESP-close-recon-2026-02.xlsx`) shows AP at **$78,000**, still flagged \"in progress.\"\n- **Variance: $2,500** (ERP higher than the workbook).\n- Per the Month-End Close Checklist (FIN-SOP-001), both AR and AP subledger tie-out are owned by **Jordan Blake**, due BD+3 \u2014 the workbook's \"Prepared by\" column confirms the same. AR is already tied and signed off; AP is the one holding up close.\n\nSubmitted via `submit_answer`:\n- `erp_ar_balance`: 128500\n- `erp_ap_balance`: 80500\n- `unreconciled_subledger`: AP\n- `variance_amount`: 2500\n- `blocking_task_owner`: Jordan Blake",
